# Ragnar OS first-boot config — OPTIONAL.
#
# Copy this file to the FAT "boot" partition of a freshly flashed card, rename
# it to exactly  ragnar.conf , and edit the values. It is read ONCE, on the
# first boot, by scripts/ragnar-firstboot.sh, then ignored.
#
# You do NOT need this file: the image boots headless with the web UI on port
# 8000, and raises its own Wi-Fi ("Ragnar" / ragnarconnect) for onboarding.
# Use it only to set a hostname or light up an attached screen unattended.

# Device hostname (also the mDNS name, so http://<hostname>.local:8000 works).
#hostname=ragnar-01

# Enable an attached display and select its driver. Omit for headless (default).
# You can also pick the display without this file: the Wi-Fi onboarding portal
# (the "Ragnar" AP page) has a screen dropdown, and the web UI's Config ->
# Display switches it later. Setting it here just makes it unattended.
# Supported driver ids (same as Config -> Display in the web UI):
#   e-Paper : epd2in13 epd2in13_V2 epd2in13_V3 epd2in13_V4 epd2in13b_V4
#             epd2in7 epd2in7_V2 epd2in9_V2 epd3in7 epd4in26
#   TFT/OLED: gc9a01 st7735s ili9486 whisplay ssd1306 lcd1602
#   LED     : max7219_8panel max7219_4panel
#display=epd2in13_V4

# To join the Tailscale mesh unattended, instead drop a separate file named
# ragnar-mesh.conf on the boot partition (see docs/mesh.md). Keep that key out
# of this file.
